=== 7. REFERENCE ONLY: did the body move while the steer swept? =======
  Everything above was measured without truth. This section
  reads the simulator's own pose and asks ONE question that
  no encoder can answer: the standstill verdict includes the
  steer count because a parked forklift steering on the spot
  could scrub its drive tyre and take the body round with it.
  Over this idle the steer axis swept while the drive count
  was held. Did the body actually rotate?

  steer axis swept over the idle       27 counts = 2.3730 deg
  TRUE position, largest excursion     0.150014 m
  TRUE heading, largest excursion      0.222052 deg
  TRUE heading, net over the idle      -0.219176 deg
  truth samples                        4200

  A true heading excursion far under the steer sweep is the
  measured answer to the scrub premise ON THIS VEHICLE, IN
  THIS SIMULATOR, ON THIS FLOOR. It is not a general result
  and it is not a licence to drop the steer term: a vehicle
  towed or pushed bodily rotates with BOTH counts held, and
  no encoder on this machine sees that at all.
  [note] this phase asserts no pass threshold on the hold. The section 5 number is the deliverable and sections 2, 3 and 6 are what attribute it.

